        "summary":  "This article presents a framework for managing agent memory in Amazon Bedrock AgentCore through three complementary lifecycle policies: TTL-based expiration, relevance decay scoring, and LLM-based consolidation. The authors provide a deployable AWS architecture using Step Functions and Lambda functions that runs nightly to prune outdated memories, score remaining ones by relevance, and merge related episodic data into compact semantic facts. The framework addresses the core problem of agents accumulating stale context that degrades response quality over time.",
