        "theme":  "Philosophy",
        "summary":  "IT leaders need hands-on experience with AI tools to effectively guide their organizations through digital transformation. The author argues that merely reading about AI or approving budgets is insufficient — leaders must personally use these tools in high-stakes work to develop the judgment necessary for strategic decision-making. This credibility gap undermines organizational trust and slows transformation efforts.",
        "execSummary":  "Leaders who approve AI budgets without personally using the tools in real work are flying blind — they lack the judgment to set realistic expectations, catch vendor hype, or make sound architectural choices. The credibility gap is not just reputational; it produces poor decisions because secondhand knowledge of AI capability is systematically optimistic. For senior customer-support or enterprise leaders, the prescription is direct: use the tools in your actual workflow for 30 days before your next strategy presentation. The leaders who will drive successful AI transformation are those who have personally hit the failure modes, not just read the case studies.",
