        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Deloitte has launched an Open Model Engineering practice to assist enterprises in balancing proprietary and open-source AI models as they build increasingly complex technology stacks. The consulting firm will hire and train forward-deployed engineers through 2027, initially focusing on Nvidia\u0027s Nemotron models while helping organizations navigate model selection, cost prediction, data sovereignty, and infrastructure deployment decisions across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific.",
        "execSummary":  "Deloitte\u0027s new Open Model Engineering practice signals that hybrid AI model strategy — mixing proprietary APIs with self-hosted open-source models — has crossed from experimentation to enterprise mainstream. The business case is data sovereignty, cost control, and reduced vendor lock-in, particularly for regulated industries or global operations with cross-border data constraints. For enterprise leaders, the practical implication is that which model is no longer a pure technology question — it is a cost, compliance, and negotiating leverage question that belongs in procurement and legal conversations. Deloitte entering this space also means competitors will soon offer equivalent practices, raising the bar for what AI strategy consulting delivers.",
