        "title":  "Fewer than 25% of enterprises have scaled AI successfully",
        "source":  "CIO Dive",
        "url":  "https://www.ciodive.com/news/rising-spend-cios-AI-success/829484/",
        "date":  "2026-09-02",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "According to Gartner\u0027s survey of over 1,300 leaders, only 22% of organizations have successfully scaled AI across multiple business units, despite 85% planning to increase AI investments. The primary obstacles include poor visibility into spending, difficulty measuring ROI, and lack of disciplined measurement tied to business outcomes.",
        "execSummary":  "Only 22% of enterprises have successfully scaled AI beyond isolated pilots — despite 85% planning to increase AI spend — and the bottleneck is measurement, not technology. Poor ROI visibility and undisciplined spending are the top failure modes, meaning the gap between AI investment and AI value is overwhelmingly a management and governance problem. For senior leaders, this is a strategic warning: scaling AI without instrumenting business outcomes first will produce more of the same failure pattern. The practical implication is to establish outcome baselines and measurement frameworks before approving the next wave of AI spend, not after.",
