        "title":  "Agentic AI is shifting the pricing models CIOs rely on",
        "source":  "CIO Dive",
        "url":  "https://www.ciodive.com/news/agentic-ai-outcome-pricing-models/829023/",
        "date":  "2026-08-31",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Enterprise software vendors are transitioning toward outcome-based pricing models where customers pay for completed tasks rather than per-seat licenses. While this shift offers improved budget predictability, adoption remains limited at approximately 19% of services agreements, with analysts projecting less than 25% adoption through 2031. CIOs must carefully negotiate outcome definitions and vendor risk-sharing arrangements to ensure these new pricing structures deliver actual value.",
        "execSummary":  "The shift from per-seat to outcome-based pricing for agentic AI tools is accelerating, and it fundamentally changes how enterprise AI contracts should be structured and audited. At only 19% adoption today, most organizations have not yet had to negotiate what a completed task means in a vendor contract — but those definitions will determine whether outcome pricing saves or wastes budget. CIOs and procurement teams need to get ahead of this now by demanding precise outcome definitions, audit rights, and vendor risk-sharing provisions before signing agentic AI agreements. The analogy to SLA negotiations in managed services is apt: the devil is entirely in the contractual definition of success.",
