        "date":  "2026-09-03",
        "theme":  "Orchestration",
        "summary":  "The article discusses how organizations can scale agentic AI from isolated pilots to enterprise-wide deployment, highlighting the need to establish clear business objectives and redesign workflows rather than layering AI onto existing processes. Governance, security, and ensuring agents have access to necessary data and backend systems are identified as essential prerequisites for scaling. The piece frames AI agents as part of the broader enterprise workforce requiring the same oversight rigor as human employees.",
        "execSummary":  "The core argument here is that agentic AI scale failures are fundamentally workflow design failures, not technology failures — organizations that layer agents onto broken or siloed processes will get broken results at scale. The workforce framing is strategically important: treating agents as workforce members subject to the same onboarding, access governance, and performance management disciplines as humans is the mental model shift that separates successful enterprise deployments from failed pilots. For senior leaders, the decision-relevant question is not are we running pilots but do we have the data access, workflow redesign, and governance infrastructure to take this pilot to 10x scale. If the answer is no, the pilot is a dead end.",
