        "source":  "MIT Technology Review",
        "url":  "https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/09/02/1142879/facilitating-ai-integration-with-simplicity-at-scale/",
        "date":  "2026-09-02",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Jabil, a global manufacturing company with over 100 sites across 30+ countries, adopted a simplify-first, then-innovate approach to technology integration. By prioritizing data consolidation and standardized workflows through SAP\u0027s integration suite, the company reduced complexity and created a foundation for AI deployment. The strategy emphasizes measurable business value, real-time supply chain visibility, and operational resilience over merely acquiring new technologies.",
        "execSummary":  "Jabil\u0027s simplify first, innovate second approach inverts the typical enterprise AI playbook and produces a more defensible outcome: AI built on consolidated, standardized data outperforms AI bolted onto fragmented legacy systems. The practical lesson for enterprise leaders is that data infrastructure investment is not a precursor to AI strategy — it is AI strategy, and organizations that treat it as a separate IT project will face the same integration failures at the AI layer that they experienced at the application layer. For customer-support leaders specifically, this translates to a clear sequencing mandate: unify your data sources and standardize your workflows before deploying AI agents, or you will automate the chaos rather than eliminate it.",
